<<<
When two or more italic letters are used, they form a single symbol, as aw, OW, ot, ah, oor, owr (cawl, cowl, coil, bah, boor, dowry).
===
When two or more italic letters are used, they form a single symbol, as *aw, ow, oi, ah, oor, owr* (c*aw*l, c*ow*l, c*oi*l, b*ah*, b*oor*, d*owr*y).
>>>

<<<
The italic symbols consisting of one vowel & r, & 00, have always a long or short mark over the first letter thus: madre, mére, mire, more, mure, pdrt, pert, port, stdol, stdod; their
===
The italic symbols consisting of one vowel & *r*, & *oo*, have always a long or short mark over the first letter thus: māre, mēre, mīre, mōre, mūre, părt, pĕrt, pŏrt, stōol, stŏod; their
>>>

